WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:06.874
"What Is GLP-1 and How Do GLP-1 Agonist Drugs
(Like Ozempic) Work?"

00:00:06.874 --> 00:00:09.042
Even over just
the last decade or so,

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:12.513
obesity rates have
spiraled out of control.

00:00:12.513 --> 00:00:16.483
Are GLP-1 receptor activators
the long-sought-after panacea

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.784
for obesity?

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:21.521
Well, first of all,
what is GLP-1?

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.690
The gastrointestinal tract
is known

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:27.728
as the largest hormone-secreting
gland in the human body,

00:00:27.728 --> 00:00:30.731
releasing more than 20
peptide hormones.

00:00:30.731 --> 00:00:33.100
About 1 out of every 100 cells

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.337
lining our entire digestive
tract acts as a nutrient sensor

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.640
and can secrete hormones
accordingly,

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:44.011
including GLP-1,
glucagon-like peptide-1.

00:00:44.011 --> 00:00:47.347
The primary stimuli
for GLP-1 secretion

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.883
are meals rich in fats
and carbohydrates,

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:54.855
and the main action of GLP-1 is
to signal nutritional abundance

00:00:54.855 --> 00:00:56.657
to the brain,
reducing our appetite

00:00:56.657 --> 00:01:00.193
so we don’t eat
too many doughnuts.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:04.264
GLP-1 also slows things down,
allowing us more time to digest,

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:07.200
and the slowing of the rate
at which food leaves our stomach

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.070
helps with blood sugar control
after a meal.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:13.106
So, GLP-1 hormone-mimicking
drugs were actually

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:16.376
first developed to treat
type 2 diabetes.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:19.580
The reason you can’t just
give people GLP-1 directly

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.815
is because it’s broken down
so quickly,

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:24.985
it hardly even makes it
one time around the circulation,

00:01:24.985 --> 00:01:29.623
thanks to inactivation
by an enzyme in our body.

00:01:29.623 --> 00:01:32.259
But then,
a compound was discovered

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:34.494
that activates GLP-1 activity

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:37.264
but was resistant
to enzyme breakdown.

00:01:37.264 --> 00:01:40.400
And it was found in a lizard.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.670
It’s a constituent
of Gila Monster venom.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.939
And the first drug was born.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:46.940
Using that as a template,

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.909
the first GLP-1 agonist
was created

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:50.711
and approved
for the treatment of diabetes

00:01:50.711 --> 00:01:53.246
about 20 years ago.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:56.216
Instead of half lasting
2.5 minutes in the body,

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.251
it lasted about 2.5 hours,

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.988
but still had to be injected
twice a day.

00:02:00.988 --> 00:02:04.224
Then came liraglutide,
which lasts all day,

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:07.527
but even once-a-day injections
can be a pain.

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:11.431
Enter semaglutide,
branded as Ozempic,

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:14.501
which could be injected
just once a week.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.970
It was approved to treat
diabetes in 2017.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.940
Within a few years, a daily oral
version had been developed,

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.908
again for diabetes,

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.810
but researchers running
those clinical trials

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.246
noticed a surprising
side effect:

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:28.548
people’s appetites diminished.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:32.019
Indeed, if you drip the hormone
GLP-1 into people’s veins,

00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:33.754
it reduces their appetite,

00:02:33.754 --> 00:02:35.789
leading
to decreased food intake.

00:02:35.789 --> 00:02:37.657
And not just a little.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:40.093
We’re talking about
a decrease in caloric intake

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:43.697
by as much as 25 to 50 percent.

00:02:43.697 --> 00:02:47.134
The GLP-1 hormone not only
slows stomach emptying--

00:02:47.134 --> 00:02:50.137
so you feel fuller longer
after eating--

00:02:50.137 --> 00:02:52.172
but also works
as an appetite suppressant

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.441
by triggering
parts of the brain

00:02:54.441 --> 00:02:57.210
responsible
for hunger and cravings.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.280
GLP-1-secreting cells don’t
only line our intestines;

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.482
they’re also in our brains.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:07.220
So, GLP-1 agonist drugs,
meaning GLP-1-mimicking drugs,

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:10.590
work kind of like
the way birth control pills do.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.827
Birth control pills mimic
placental hormones,

00:03:13.827 --> 00:03:15.295
thereby tricking our body

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.697
into thinking we’re pregnant
all the time.

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:20.467
Ozempic-type drugs mimic GLP-1,

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:21.635
thereby tricking our body

00:03:21.635 --> 00:03:24.071
into thinking
we’re eating all the time;

00:03:24.071 --> 00:03:26.540
so, it dials down
our hunger drive.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:28.475
In 2021, semaglutide,

00:03:28.475 --> 00:03:30.744
originally approved as Ozempic
to treat diabetes,

00:03:30.744 --> 00:03:35.315
was rebranded at a higher dose
as Wegovy to treat obesity,

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:39.686
and the weight-loss industry
changed overnight,

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.755
shifting away
from meal replacements

00:03:41.755 --> 00:03:43.623
and portion-control plans

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.959
to the new world
of private equity-funded

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.227
telemedicine entities

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:50.097
set up to offer these
injectable weight-loss drugs.

00:03:50.097 --> 00:03:53.233
Even Weight Watchers has openly
embraced these kinds of drugs

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.102
as the future of weight loss.

00:03:55.102 --> 00:03:58.138
They were even approved
for kids as young as age 12--

00:03:58.138 --> 00:04:00.040
tweens, not even teens.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.708
Is that a good idea?

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.343
What are the pros and cons

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:05.278
of these new
weight-loss medications?

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:09.516
That’s just what I’ll cover
next.

